[{"category":"section","location":"api/#API","page":"API","text":"Submitters using DistSSHKitQueue or julia -m DistSSHKitQueue submit go …. Queue code using DistSSHKit. Job files for Kit go still do not import DistSSHKit.\n\nCLI: setup / teardown -y / submit go / submit drive / status / watch / cancel. Prefer julia -m DistSSHKitQueue. Julia: submit!(q, script, hosts...; kind=:drive). Waiter: DistSSHKit 0.4.1+ execute!(…; detached=true, job_id=…). Placement tokens are parent[:N] / child:NAME[:N]. Config: ~/.distsshkitqueue/config.toml.","title":"API"},{"category":"module","location":"api/#DistSSHKitQueue.DistSSHKitQueue","page":"API","text":"DistSSHKitQueue — FIFO waiter for DistSSHKit (go / drive).\n\nPackage entry: exports, includes, main (@main on Julia 1.12+). FIFO: src/DistSSHKitQueue/. Client CLI: src/client/. Queue host CLI: src/qhost/. Waiter runs DistSSHKit execute!(...; detached=true). --project=<queue-env> loads this package; the job tree is job_project(). Config: ~/.distsshkitqueue/config.toml.\n\nConcept and design notes: README.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DistSSHKitQueue.DistSSHKitQueue"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#DistSSHKitQueue.Queue","page":"API","text":"FIFO table: one DistSSHKit job at a time. Placement tokens are Kit's, not a Queue ceiling.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DistSSHKitQueue.Queue"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#DistSSHKitQueue.Job","page":"API","text":"One table row. hosts are DistSSHKit 0.4 tokens (parent[:N] / child:NAME[:N]). kwargs is an opaque bag for DistSSHKit execute! (project is the job tree).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DistSSHKitQueue.Job"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#DistSSHKitQueue.submit!","page":"API","text":"Enqueue. kind=:go or :drive (DistSSHKit execute!).\n\nhosts must be DistSSHKit 0.4 placement tokens (parent[:N] / child:NAME[:N]). Missing project uses job_project() (cwd / DISTRIBUTED_PROJECT_ROOT), not the waiter --project. Same verb as CLI submit.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DistSSHKitQueue.submit!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#DistSSHKitQueue.cancel!","page":"API","text":"Cancel :queued, or :running via DistSSHKit terminate_run! when result_path / output_dir is known.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DistSSHKitQueue.cancel!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#DistSSHKitQueue.serve!","page":"API","text":"Load store (stale :running → :failed), then step! until interrupt. Ctrl-C stops the waiter, not Kit.\n\nA second serve on the same store prints Already running and returns.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DistSSHKitQueue.serve!"},{"category":"section","location":"#DistSSHKitQueue.jl","page":"Introduction","text":"warning: Under construction. Do not use this.\n\n\nSmall-lab job queue on DistSSHKit.jl.\n\nDistSSHKit runs one job (go / drive). DistSSHKitQueue is a long-lived waiter (FIFO, one table job).\n\nThis package is not on General yet. See the README for the concept diagram.","title":"DistSSHKitQueue.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#CLI","page":"Introduction","text":"Client (dev laptop):\n\njulia --project=. -m DistSSHKitQueue --qhost HOST status\njulia --project=. -m DistSSHKitQueue --qhost HOST watch\njulia --project=. -m DistSSHKitQueue --qhost HOST submit go child:worker:4 SCRIPT.jl\njulia --project=. -m DistSSHKitQueue --qhost HOST cancel <id>\n\nQueue host (always-on):\n\njulia -m DistSSHKitQueue setup\njulia -m DistSSHKitQueue serve\njulia -m DistSSHKitQueue enable\njulia -m DistSSHKitQueue teardown -y\n\n--qhost is client-only. setup / serve / enable / disable refuse it. Omit --qhost only when you are already on the queue host (not a sleeping laptop). status / watch print that qhost (or local plus hostname). submit auto-starts the waiter. The waiter calls DistSSHKit execute!(…; detached=true, job_id=…).","title":"CLI"},{"category":"section","location":"#Installation","page":"Introduction","text":"From a checkout:\n\npkg> dev /path/to/DistSSHKitQueue.jl\n\nNeeds DistSSHKit 0.4.1+ from General (a hard dependency; do not Pkg.develop Kit for ordinary Queue work), Julia 1.12+, plus ssh / rsync / git as in DistSSHKit.","title":"Installation"},{"category":"section","location":"#Contributing","page":"Introduction","text":"Bugs and features: Issues. See CONTRIBUTING.md.","title":"Contributing"}]
